---
import BlogLayout from '../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro';
import CopyButton from '../../components/CopyButton.astro';
import { authoredBlogMetadata, formatBlogDate } from '../../data/blogPresentation';
import { createBreadcrumbSchema, productFacts } from '../../data/productFacts';

const title = 'Test Secret Manager and Cloud KMS Locally Without IAM';
const description = 'Eliminate plaintext .env workarounds in development. Exercise Secret Manager versions and Cloud KMS cryptographic workflows locally using standard GCP SDKs.';
const pageUrl = new URL('blog/local-secrets-kms-without-iam-friction/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString();
const metadata = authoredBlogMetadata['local-secrets-kms-without-iam-friction'];
const contents = [
  { id: 'problem', label: 'The .env divergence trap in cloud apps' },
  { id: 'solution', label: 'Real Secret Manager and KMS APIs on localhost' },
  { id: 'workflows', label: 'What security workflows you can verify' },
  { id: 'try-it', label: 'Start security services and inspect secrets' },
  { id: 'production', label: 'Keep production keys strictly out of local files' },
];
const secStart = `localcloud start --local-only --services secretmanager,kms
eval "$(localcloud env)"`;
const secSeed = `services:
  secretmanager:
    secrets:
      - name: stripe-webhook-secret
        versions:
          - data: fake-local-webhook-secret-v1`;
const structuredData = [
  createBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: productFacts.siteUrl },
    { name: 'Blog', url: new URL('blog/', productFacts.siteUrl).toString() },
    { name: title, url: pageUrl },
  ]),
];
---

<BlogLayout {title} {description} {structuredData} {contents} article={{ publishedAt: metadata.publishedAt, headline: title }}>
  <Fragment slot="hero">
    <article class="site-section site-section--hero">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <nav class="mb-5 text-sm text-[var(--text-2)]" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/blog/">Blog</a></nav>
        <span class="site-eyebrow">Security Workflows</span>
        <h1 class="mt-5">{title}</h1>
        <p class="blog-meta"><span>Published <time datetime={metadata.publishedAt}>{formatBlogDate(metadata.publishedAt)}</time></span><span>{metadata.minutes} min read</span><span>{metadata.topic}</span></p>
        <p class="blog-deck">Many apps use Secret Manager and Cloud KMS in production, then bypass both with plaintext <code>.env</code> branches locally—leaving secret rotation, version resolution, and envelope crypto code untested until deployment.</p>
        <div class="blog-actions">
          <a class="site-button site-button--primary" href="/services/secret-manager/">Secret Manager guide</a>
          <a href="/services/cloud-kms/">Cloud KMS guide</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="site-section">
    <div class="container container--narrow space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 id="problem">The .env divergence trap in cloud apps</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Because setting up KMS key rings and Secret Manager IAM roles for every developer workstation takes effort, teams often add an <code>if os.getenv("ENV") == "local"</code> shortcut that reads plaintext environment variables instead.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">That shortcut means secret-version lookup paths, missing-version error handling, and KMS encrypt/decrypt wrappers never run locally before hitting staging.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="solution">Real Secret Manager and KMS APIs on localhost</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">LocalCloud implements <a href="/services/secret-manager/">Secret Manager</a> and <a href="/services/cloud-kms/">Cloud KMS</a> directly through its shared gateway (<code>2 ms</code> p50 secret read latency). Your application deletes the local-only bypass and exercises the exact same SDK client code in dev, CI, and production.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="workflows">What security workflows you can verify</h2>
        <ul class="site-list mt-5">
          <li><strong>Secret versions &amp; rotation:</strong> Create secrets, add multiple payload versions, disable older versions, and test <code>latest</code> resolution.</li>
          <li><strong>Envelope encryption:</strong> Create key rings and symmetric/asymmetric keys in local KMS to verify encrypt, decrypt, and sign calls in application code.</li>
          <li><strong>Seeded startup secrets:</strong> Pre-populate synthetic secrets via <code>seed.yaml</code> so services boot without manual CLI setup.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="try-it">Start security services and inspect secrets</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Enable <code>secretmanager</code> and <code>kms</code>, seed synthetic secret versions via <a href="/docs/seed-data/">Seed Data</a>, and browse secret metadata in the <a href="/docs/console/">Web Console</a>. See <a href="/docs/">Getting Started</a> for CLI installation.</p>
        <div class="site-panel mt-5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <span class="site-kicker">Start security services</span>
            <CopyButton text={secStart} analyticsLabel="copy-blog-sec-start" />
          </div>
          <pre><code>{secStart}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="site-panel mt-5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <span class="site-kicker">secrets-seed.yaml (synthetic values only)</span>
            <CopyButton text={secSeed} analyticsLabel="copy-blog-sec-seed" />
          </div>
          <pre><code>{secSeed}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 id="production">Keep production keys strictly out of local files</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Always populate local Secret Manager and KMS instances with synthetic test values only, keep ports bound with <code>--local-only</code>, and validate hardware HSM policies and real IAM enforcement in Google Cloud before release.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BlogLayout>
